# Every fixture under this directory is read byte-for-byte (golden-comparison
# JSON/markdown, and pages whose md5 is asserted against a recorded value).
# This repo checks out with core.autocrlf=true on Windows, which silently
# rewrites LF to CRLF on any checkout that "touches" a text-attributed file
# (see Tools/lib/purpose-header.mjs's own BYTE-EXACTNESS note at :28-32 for
# the same hazard elsewhere in this tree) and would invalidate every hash
# below. Marking the whole directory binary opts it out of that conversion.
#
# An attribute is only honoured once it is in effect. The apply that CREATED
# this file wrote its seven siblings with conversion still on, so they landed
# CRLF, and they stay CRLF: `git apply` writes a postimage with the line
# endings the target file already has, so no patch can put them back. What
# makes that harmless is that the spec normalises line endings before it
# compares or hashes anything, so its assertions read the CONTENT rather than
# the convention — and the byteLength recorded in each sheet-index.json is
# the normalised one, which is the length the collector measures.
#
# -text does not stop a FORMATTER. The pre-commit hook runs prettier --write
# over staged .md/.html/.mjs (lint-staged.config.js), after the gates a lane
# reports; it padded golden-summary.md's tables and reflowed both pages, and
# the spec was red on main until the bytes were restored. The directory is
# listed in .prettierignore for that reason, and
# Tools/wave-end-contact-sheet-index.spec.mjs asks prettier itself whether
# every file here is still covered.
* -text
